      "body": "## Bevy version\r\n4ce37395da029eb8b58c78c32812fe8329a3a1a4\r\n\r\n## \\[Optional\\] Relevant system information\r\n\r\nIf you cannot get Bevy to build or run on your machine, please include:\r\nRust version: 1.69.0\r\nLinux 6.3.5-arch1-1, Gnome (tried both on Wayland and Xorg)\r\n```\r\nAdapterInfo { name: \"NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1050\", vendor: 4318, device: 7309, device_type: DiscreteGpu, driver: \"NVIDIA\", driver_info: \"530.41.03\", backend: Vulkan }\r\n```\r\n## What you did\r\n`cargo run --example 3d_shapes`\r\n## What went wrong\r\nGot an error:\r\n```\r\n2023-06-01T04:49:14.980085Z ERROR wgpu_hal::vulkan::instance: VALIDATION [UNASSIGNED-CoreValidation-Shader-InconsistentSpirv (0x6bbb14)]\r\n\tValidation Error: [ UNASSIGNED-CoreValidation-Shader-InconsistentSpirv ] Object 0: handle = 0x55d1a59495d0, type = VK_OBJECT_TYPE_DEVICE; | MessageID = 0x6bbb14 | SPIR-V module not valid: [VUID-StandaloneSpirv-OpTypeRuntimeArray-04680] Vulkan, OpTypeStruct containing an OpTypeRuntimeArray must be decorated with Block or BufferBlock.\r\n  %PointLights = OpTypeStruct %_runtimearr_PointLight\r\n\r\n```\r\nThe program seems to run completely fine and everything looks correct.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\nrunning `cargo run --example sprite` for example doesn't have any errors, only the 3d examples (tested `3d_shapes`, `3d_rotation` and `3d_scene`)\r\n",
